<title>UK: Clarke expects EMU progress report at Ecofin.</title>
<headline>Clarke expects EMU progress report at Ecofin.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>British Chancellor of the Exchequer Kenneth Clarke said on Monday he expected the meeting of European Union finance ministers (ECOFIN) on December 2 to put together a progress report on EMU for the Dublin summit.</p>
<p>&quot;What I am anticipating as the most likely thing to come from ECOFIN is a report to go ahead to the summit (on December 13 and 14) at Dublin on where we are on discussions on all these things (concerning EMU),&quot; Clarke told parliament.</p>
</text>
